,"followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-15T12:53:57Z","updated_at":"2025-11-15T12:53:57Z","body":"Dupe of https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111666","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3536462979/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3537194950","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112756#issuecomment-3537194950","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112756","id":3537194950,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7S1U_G","user":{"login":"okaysalmon","id":238761286,"node_id":"U_kgDODjs1Rg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/238761286?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon","html_url":"https://github.com/okaysalmon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-16T00:36:56Z","updated_at":"2025-11-16T01:03:19Z","body":"> Dupe of [#111666](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111666)\n\nI don't think this is a duplicate of that issue.\n\nBut the issue isn't what I thought I was in the first place. This is an issue of the basis.get_scale() returned value being affected by rotation when it's not meant to.\n\nEven though the returned Vector3's are equals, they are not valued as the same. ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3537194950/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3537341088","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112756#issuecomment-3537341088","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112756","id":3537341088,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7S14qg","user":{"login":"okaysalmon","id":238761286,"node_id":"U_kgDODjs1Rg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/238761286?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon","html_url":"https://github.com/okaysalmon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-16T01:48:43Z","updated_at":"2025-11-16T01:48:43Z","body":"this is with basis print outs too\n\n<img width=\"1338\" height=\"651\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6abe0bc2-5f6b-4ff7-abc9-20393d32236f\" />","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3537341088/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3537503427","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112756#issuecomment-3537503427","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112756","id":3537503427,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7S2gTD","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-16T03:00:41Z","updated_at":"2025-11-16T03:00:41Z","body":"So are you talking about the issue where rotation changes the scale obtained from the basis matrix? That is not a problem with the SkeletonModifier.\n\nThere are two scales obtainable from the matrix, global_scale and local_scale. Of course, rotation changes the global_scale.\n\nAt this time, the local_scale obtained from the matrix may be affected by rotation due to precision errors.\n\nWhen rotating a matrix containing scale, we try to avoid this issue as much as possible by evicting the scale, rotating the normalized matrix, and then restoring the scale. However, even then, errors may occur at high precision.\n\nFYI, as a fundamental property of matrices, negative scale values represented as Vector3 cannot be distinguished from rotation, so the sign tends not to be preserved. The issue with negative scale applies also to 2D, and this is [documented](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_node2d.html#class-node2d-property-scale).\n\nIn any case, considering scaling in IK is generally not recommended. Especially when the parent Node or parent Bone has non-uniform scaling, it causes global shear on the child, then rotation changes the rendered bone length.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3537503427/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3537768998","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112756#issuecomment-3537768998","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112756","id":3537768998,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7S3hIm","user":{"login":"okaysalmon","id":238761286,"node_id":"U_kgDODjs1Rg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/238761286?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon","html_url":"https://github.com/okaysalmon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-16T04:54:43Z","updated_at":"2025-11-16T04:55:16Z","body":"The issue is from basis.get_scale()\n\nIn the documentation it states rotation will not effect scale, but it dose.\n\nThis is not restricted to bones the minimal reproduction I have put up in my previous comments showing this with a mesh3d.\n\nEven though the return vectors representing scale are a match. They show as not being a match.\n\nIf rotatation is know to effect the scale return then this should be noted on the function get_scale() rather then it stating that it dose not effect it.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3537768998/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3538474430","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112756#issuecomment-3538474430","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112756","id":3538474430,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7S6NW-","user":{"login":"okaysalmon","id":238761286,"node_id":"U_kgDODjs1Rg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/238761286?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon","html_url":"https://github.com/okaysalmon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-16T09:55:02Z","updated_at":"2025-11-16T09:55:02Z","body":"Here is a link to the doc's showing rotation should not effect the basis.get_scale()\n\nhttps://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_basis.html#class-basis-method-get-scale\n\nHowever as per the above it dose, as a rotated node, when it has its scale compared with the previous scale (even though they both print out to uniform scales) will show as not equal.\n\nIt was this error that made me think there was an issue within the skeletonModifier3D but it's not.\n\nIn my project I have made modifications to my code to get round the flick effect, by just having it rebuild the 2D arrays length values and not reconstructing the full array on scale changes. \n\nHowever the documentation should be updated to let people know that the rotation may effect the scale even though they may show the same values, when compared directly with another get_scale of equil value there may be a minuscule diffrance that make the comparison show as false when you would expect true ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3538474430/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3539424082","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112756#issuecomment-3539424082","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112756","id":3539424082,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7S91NS","user":{"login":"okaysalmon","id":238761286,"node_id":"U_kgDODjs1Rg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/238761286?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon","html_url":"https://github.com/okaysalmon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okaysalmon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-16T22:23:30Z","updated_at":"2025-11-16T22:23:30Z","body":"For anyone who comes across this issue in the future and stumbles upon this while trying to figure out how to fix it,\nyou can do the following:\n\nWhen you’re creating the initial variable to be saved:\n\n`@onready var global_scale: String = str(self.global_transform.basis.get_scale())`\n\n\nThen, where you make the comparison:\n\n```\nfunc _process(delta: float) -> void:\n\tvar current_global_scale: String = str(self.global_transform.basis.get_scale())\n\tif global_scale != current_global_scale:\n\t\t#do stuff\n\n```\n\nThis converts the scale value to a string, and when compared as strings, it filters out micro adjustments.\nThe limitation with this approach is that very small scale changes will not be detected, however, this is what prevents rotations from affecting the result, since those minute floating-point changes are ignored.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3539424082/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]